                  EXCEPTIONS TO INVERSION RACEMIZATION

1. QUATERNARY AMMONIUM SALTS ($N^+ R_1 R_2 R_3 R_4 X^-$): Lacks a non-bonding lone pair;
   rigid $sp^3$ tetrahedral geometry preserves optical activity ($\text{Chiral}$).
2. CYCLIC / RIGID AMINES (*e.g., Tröger's Base*): Ring strain prevents planar $sp^2$ transition state;
   resolvable into stable $d$- and $l$-enantiomers.
